WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.263
This is where HR starts to drive identity,
for a first, limited group of people.

2
00:00:05.263 --> 00:00:06.513
The order matters.

3
00:00:06.513 --> 00:00:11.050
The feed is named as one of the
agency's HR integration points.

4
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.507
The attribute authority map is signed,

5
00:00:13.507 --> 00:00:17.423
and HR data is checked against
reality and fixed at the source,

6
00:00:17.423 --> 00:00:22.337
because a drifted feed produces drifted
access faster than any ticket queue.

7
00:00:22.337 --> 00:00:27.025
Joiner, mover and leaver are proven
end to end in a test tenant.

8
00:00:27.025 --> 00:00:29.446
Then the pilot group runs in shadow mode,

9
00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:33.240
where the feed shows what it would
do, before it's allowed to act.
